  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Determine the number of surjective functions from $X$ to $Y$ given that:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$X=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $Y=\\{1,2,3\\}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6$",
          "worked": "Every element of $Y$ must occur as an image. Since both sets have three elements, each image occurs exactly once. There are three choices for the first image, two for the second and one for the third.\n$$3\\times2\\times1=6.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$X=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "Three inputs can produce at most three distinct images, so they cannot cover the four elements of $Y$. Therefore, there are no surjective functions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$X=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ and $Y=\\{1,2,3\\}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$36$\n\nChoose the two inputs sharing an image, then assign the three distinct images.",
          "worked": "To cover all three elements of $Y$, exactly two inputs share an image and the other two have different images. Choose the pair of inputs in $\\binom{4}{2}=6$ ways. Choose their common image in three ways, then assign the remaining images to the remaining inputs in two ways.\n$$6\\times3\\times2=36.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
